<title>POLAND: Poland sells PLN 698 mln fixed bonds at tender.</title>
<headline>Poland sells PLN 698 mln fixed bonds at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland sold 146 million zlotys of 15-percent two-year fixed bonds and 552 million zlotys of 12-percent five-year bonds at today's tender, the public debt department of the finance ministry said.  </p>
<p>		     15-PCT TWO-YEAR	12-PCT FIVE-YEAR</p>
<p> min price	  90.60 (92.90)	    79.30 (79.90)</p>
<p> avg price	  90.77 (93.17)	    79.61 (79.92)</p>
<p> max price	  92.00			79.82</p>
<p> joint offer			  800</p>
<p> bids recorded    323.4			619.2</p>
<p> bids accepted    146.2			551.9</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys. Figures in brackets are from the previous auction of similar bonds, on January 16, 1997.    -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
